AWS RDS Backup and Restore Automation
A complete guide and automation record for taking an Amazon RDS instance snapshot and restoring it to a new instance for database infrastructure updates and validation.

Architecture & Task Overview
Source RDS Instance: datacenter-rds

Snapshot Identifier: datacenter-snapshot

Restored RDS Instance: datacenter-snapshot-restore

Target Instance Class: db.t3.micro

AWS Region: us-east-1

Implementation Steps & Commands
1. Verify Source Instance Status
Ensure the source RDS instance is available before initiating backup tasks.

Bash
aws rds describe-db-instances \
    --db-instance-identifier datacenter-rds \
    --region us-east-1 \
    --query "DBInstances[0].DBInstanceStatus"
2. Create the Database Snapshot
Capture a manual snapshot of the production-aligned instance.

Bash
aws rds create-db-snapshot \
    --db-instance-identifier datacenter-rds \
    --db-snapshot-identifier datacenter-snapshot \
    --region us-east-1
3. Wait for Snapshot Completion
Monitor the snapshot creation process until it reaches the available state.

Bash
aws rds wait db-snapshot-available \
    --db-snapshot-identifier datacenter-snapshot \
    --region us-east-1
4. Restore Snapshot to New Instance
Provision a new RDS instance using the captured snapshot and assign the db.t3.micro instance class.

Bash
aws rds restore-db-instance-from-db-snapshot \
    --db-instance-identifier datacenter-snapshot-restore \
    --db-snapshot-identifier datacenter-snapshot \
    --db-instance-class db.t3.micro \
    --region us-east-1
5. Verify Restored Instance Availability
Confirm that the newly restored instance successfully transitions to the available state.

Bash
aws rds wait db-instance-available \
    --db-instance-identifier datacenter-snapshot-restore \
    --region us-east-1
